  "description": "\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tDecomposeRL Tiny-Judge: Distillation Data\n\t\n\n\n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tOverview\n\t\n\nDecomposeRL Tiny-Judge is the distillation dataset used to train DecomposeRL's tiny-judge stack \u2014 eight small ModernBERT-large classifier heads that replace a Qwen3-32B LLM judge as the reward model during GRPO training.\nEach row is a judgment task instance: a text input (claim / question / answer / evidence, depending on the task) paired with a label distilled from a Qwen/Qwen3-32B judge call\u2026 See the full description on the dataset page: https://huggingface.co/datasets/dipta007/decomposeRL-tiny-judge.",
